  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **K-Means++ Initialization** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_kmeans_plusplus(X: list, k: int, initial_center_index: int = 0) -> list:\n    data = np.array(X, dtype=float)\n    centers = [data[initial_center_index]]\n    while len(centers) < k:\n        c_arr = np.array(centers)\n        dists = np.min(np.sum((data[:, np.newaxis, :] - c_arr[np.newaxis, :, :]) ** 2, axis=2), axis=1)\n        centers.append(data[int(np.argmax(dists))])\n    return np.round(centers, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
